### ======================================================================================
### ============ Status changes – task 3.5. Run --seed first; logins: Noa, Yael (24, Admin + Handler, central HR), Ron ============
### ======================================================================================
### PATCH /status { newStatus, rowVersion, reason?, message? }. message = a comment the employee sees (required for
### WaitingForEmployee and Resolved); reason = internal (staff timeline only), handlers only. Every change sends the
### rowVersion the user saw (from GET /api/tickets/{id}); a newer one → 409. The ticket ids below are the first new ones
### after --seed (201, 202, 203) – adjust if you opened other tickets before.

### Noa
# @name s35Noa
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "noa.berkovich@example.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Yael – handler in central HR (the fallback category's department)
# @name s35Yael
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "yael.harpaz@example.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

### ---------- Full cycle: start → request info → the employee replies → resolve → confirm ----------

### 1. Noa opens a ticket (→ GENERAL, central HR, Assigned) → 201 { id: 201 }
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Noa.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=b35

--b35
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="subject"

בדיקת מחזור סטטוסים
--b35
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

לא קיבלתי את תלוש השכר של החודש
--b35--

### 2. Yael reads it → allowedActions incl. "start" (in her department's queue, or hers)
# @name c1
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Yael.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 2a. If assignedTo is another handler: Yael takes it (POST /assign with a reason) and reads it again (step 2)
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Yael.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "targetUserId": 24, "reason": "לוקחת לטיפולי", "rowVersion": "{{c1.response.body.$.rowVersion}}" }

### 3. "התחל טיפול": Assigned → InProgress (from the queue it also assigns Yael – a "Taken" change row)
# @name c2
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201/status
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Yael.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "InProgress", "rowVersion": "{{c1.response.body.$.rowVersion}}" }

### 4. The old version again → 409 "הפנייה עודכנה על ידי משתמש אחר"
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201/status
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Yael.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "WaitingForEmployee", "message": "x", "rowVersion": "{{c1.response.body.$.rowVersion}}" }

### 5. "בקש מידע" without a message → 400 errors.message
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201/status
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Yael.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "WaitingForEmployee", "rowVersion": "{{c2.response.body.$.rowVersion}}" }

### 6. "בקש מידע": InProgress → WaitingForEmployee; the message is a visible comment, the reason staff-only.
### The SLA clock pauses (SlaPausedAt) – the ticket is not overdue while waiting.
# @name c3
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201/status
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Yael.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "WaitingForEmployee", "message": "נא לצרף את פרטי חשבון הבנק", "reason": "חסר מסמך", "rowVersion": "{{c2.response.body.$.rowVersion}}" }

### 7. Noa replies → 201; the ticket is back InProgress automatically (history: changedByName null = "מערכת"),
### and DueAt moved by the time waited (compare dueAt in GET /201 before and after)
POST {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Noa.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=b35

--b35
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="body"

מצרפת את הפרטים: בנק לאומי, סניף 800
--b35--

### 8. Yael reads the new version
# @name c4
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Yael.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 9. "שלח פתרון": InProgress → Resolved; the message is saved as the resolution reply (isResolution), ResolvedAt set
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201/status
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Yael.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "Resolved", "message": "התלוש נשלח שוב לכתובת המייל שלך.", "rowVersion": "{{c4.response.body.$.rowVersion}}" }

### 10. Noa reads it → allowedActions ["reply", "confirmResolved", "reopen"] and rowVersion
# @name c5
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Noa.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 11. A reason from the requester → 400 errors.reason
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201/status
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Noa.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "Closed", "reason": "פנימי", "rowVersion": "{{c5.response.body.$.rowVersion}}" }

### 12. "הבעיה נפתרה": Resolved → Closed (ClosedAt). The employee's history has no reasons; the staff history (below) does.
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201/status
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Noa.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "Closed", "rowVersion": "{{c5.response.body.$.rowVersion}}" }

###
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201/history
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Yael.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### ---------- Reopening (within 7 days of the resolution) ----------
### Open ticket 202 as in step 1, start it (step 3) and resolve it (step 9) with its own versions, then:

### Noa reads it
# @name r1
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/202
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Noa.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### "פתיחה מחדש": Resolved → InProgress with an optional message; a new DueAt from now by the urgency (none → Medium),
### ResolvedAt cleared (the previous one stays in the history). After 7 days → 422 "reopen-window-expired".
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/202/status
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Noa.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "InProgress", "message": "הבעיה חזרה אחרי יומיים", "rowVersion": "{{r1.response.body.$.rowVersion}}" }

### ---------- Cancelling ----------
### Open ticket 203 as in step 1, then:

# @name x1
GET {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/203
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Noa.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Noa cancels (New / Assigned only) → 200; comments afterwards → 422 "ticket-closed"
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/203/status
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Noa.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "Cancelled", "rowVersion": "{{x1.response.body.$.rowVersion}}" }

### ---------- Errors ----------

### Ron (department manager) → 403 "status-change-not-allowed" (spec 14, question 8); the executive likewise
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/201/status
Authorization: Bearer {{staffRon.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "Resolved", "message": "x", "rowVersion": "AAAAAAAAAAA=" }

### The requester tries a handler's transition (Assigned → InProgress) → 422 "invalid-status-transition";
### a colleague on another handler's ticket → 422 "ticket-assigned-to-other"
PATCH {{API_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/203/status
Authorization: Bearer {{s35Noa.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "InProgress", "rowVersion": "{{x1.response.body.$.rowVersion}}" }

### Auto-close (AutoCloseResolvedWorker, every AutoClose:IntervalMinutes): Resolved for 7 days → Closed by "מערכת".
### To see it locally: resolve a ticket, then UPDATE Tickets SET ResolvedAt = DATEADD(day, -8, SYSUTCDATETIME()) WHERE Id = ...,
### set AutoClose:IntervalMinutes to 1 and restart the API.

